<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{T}(v_{i})=\{v_{i-1},v_{i+1},v_{i1},\dots,v_{ik}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{T}(v_{i})=\{v_{i-1},v_{i+1},v_{i1},\dots,v_{ik}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for the path <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}v_{i1},v_{i}v_{i2},\dots,v_{i}v_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}v_{i1},v_{i}v_{i2},\dots,v_{i}v_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>, we notice that <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{irr}(T)-\operatorname{irr}(T^{\prime})&gt;\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>irr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>irr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{irr}(T)-\operatorname{irr}(T^{\prime})&gt;\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">A path <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has degrees <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(v_{1})=\deg_{T}(v_{k})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(v_{1})=\deg_{T}(v_{k})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(v_{2})=\dots=\deg_{T}(v_{k-1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(v_{2})=\dots=\deg_{T}(v_{k-1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{irr}(\mathcal{P}_{n})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>irr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{irr}(\mathcal{P}_{n})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by considering <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathcal{T}_{n,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathcal{T}_{n,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{irr}(T)\geq\operatorname{irr}(\mathcal{P}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>irr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>irr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{irr}(T)\geq\operatorname{irr}(\mathcal{P}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cong\mathcal{P}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cong\mathcal{P}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
