<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bipartite graph , let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be the first Zagreb index. Then,</span></p>
</div>
